<div class="wrap rows">
  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="what-title">
    <h2 id="what-title">What ADAS calibration is</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>ADAS stands for Advanced Driver Assistance Systems: lane departure warning, lane-keeping assist, automatic emergency braking, adaptive cruise control, traffic sign recognition, and automatic high beams. Most of them depend on a forward-facing camera mounted at the top of your windshield.</p>
      <p>That camera has to look at the road from exactly the angle the manufacturer designed. When the windshield is replaced, the camera is taken off and put back on new glass, and even a tiny change in angle can throw it off. Calibration re-aims the camera so the system sees lanes, cars, and distances correctly again.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="need-title">
    <h2 id="need-title">Does my vehicle need it?</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>If your vehicle has a camera behind the rearview mirror, it almost always needs calibration after a windshield replacement. Signs you have one:</p>
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>A camera housing</strong> on the windshield behind the rearview mirror.</li>
        <li><strong>Lane departure or lane-keeping</strong> warnings or steering assist.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatic emergency braking</strong> or forward collision warning.</li>
        <li><strong>Adaptive cruise control</strong> that keeps a set distance from the car ahead.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Send us your VIN when you ask for a quote and we'll tell you up front whether your vehicle needs calibration and include it in the price. A <a href="/windshield-repair/">chip repair</a> leaves the camera alone, so it doesn't need calibration.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="types-title">
    <h2 id="types-title">Static and dynamic calibration</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>Manufacturers call for one of two methods, and some vehicles need both:</p>
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Static calibration</strong> is done with the vehicle parked. We set up targets at precise distances in front of the vehicle and calibrate the camera to them using a scan tool.</li>
        <li><strong>Dynamic calibration</strong> is done on the road. The scan tool puts the camera into calibration mode and we drive at set speeds on clearly marked roads until the system finishes learning.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We follow the method your vehicle's manufacturer specifies, not whichever one is quicker.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row row-dark" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <h2 id="how-title">How we do it, in one visit</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Pre-scan.</strong> We check your vehicle's safety systems for existing faults before any work starts.</li>
        <li><strong>Glass work.</strong> Your <a href="/windshield-replacement/">windshield is replaced</a> with proper urethane and curing.</li>
        <li><strong>Calibrate.</strong> The camera is recalibrated on our own equipment to the manufacturer's procedure.</li>
        <li><strong>Post-scan and verify.</strong> A final scan confirms the system is calibrated with no faults, and you get the documentation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Most glass companies replace the windshield and send you to a dealership to finish the job. We don't, so there's no second appointment and no driving around with safety systems that may not work right.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-light" href="/contact/#quote">Ask if your vehicle needs calibration</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="warranty-title">
    <h2 id="warranty-title">Backed by our warranty</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>ADAS calibrations are warranted for 30 days. If your camera needs to be recalibrated within 30 days because of our calibration, we'll redo it at no charge. See the full warranty on our <a href="/faq/">FAQ page</a>.</p>
